        "evidence": "cemetery-group-emergence.md:1-17 the conjecture is the non-trivial monotonicity τ(M_{β≤k·w'})=0 for every continuation. CemeteryGroupEmergence.lean:44-45 encodes monotone_under_extension as ∀ T, inCemetery (nodeOf T) → tauImage T = 0, but the only provided instance (lean:75-80) makes tauImage≡0, so the downstream 'theorems' tauImage_eq_zero_of_inCemetery (lean:52-57) and killSwitch_zero_mul (lean:67-72) are proved against a model where τ is identically zero — they establish nothing about the actual observation functor.",
        "notes": "Lean proves a vacuously-implied version: the conditional 'theorems' hold for the trivial τ≡0 instance, diverging from the .md claim that τ genuinely annihilates only cemetery extensions. The §3b-cond pattern requires the class field to carry the genuine sub-hypotheses and the instance to be honest (sorry); here the instance trivializes the hypothesis. proof-statement-integrity fail: the formal artifact does not derive the narrative claim, it satisfies it by a degenerate model."
